    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=89df2234-abda-481d-9d9f-d75161691110&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201994083771_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Supervisor Clinico",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-03\n\nLocation: San Juan\n\nThe clinical supervisor is responsible for directing and managing an effective clinical psychology service delivered by doctoral-level clinical psychology students using applicable principles of health psychology and substance use disorders.  He/She will perform other duties as assigned by the Program Director such as: Responsibilities: Lead clinical supervision of doctoral students.  Participate in training sessions and workshops to enhance treatment skills.  Prepare and maintain supervision process documents, case histories, and reports.  Follows up to determine reliability and validity of treatment used by doctoral students.  Lead recommendations regarding modification to services and service delivery.  Supervise and review patients’ treatment plan developed by doctoral-level students.  Facilitates the overall development and implementation of comprehensive, individualized plan of treatment in conjunction with doctoral-level students.  Promote consultation skills in primary care settings. Participate, when appropriate, in multidisciplinary team case discussions. Education:  PsyD or PhD degree in clinical psychology.     Requirements and skills: Knowledge of assessment and evidence-based treatment for substance use disorders.  Computer literate with Windows 10, Microsoft 365, Smartsheet or Excel. Skills in organizing resources and establishing priorities.  Available to work flexible times.  Ability to collaborate with people of different educational backgrounds, cultures, and roles Ability to solve different problems which may arise during the project.  Problem solving skills.  Time management skills.  Effective writing and verbal communication skills.  Available to move to a variety of clinical settings The statements mentioned here are intended to describe the general functions of the position.  This is not intended to be an exhaustive list of all the responsibilities and skills of personnel classified to this position. Albizu is an Equal Opportunity / Affirmative Action Employer with a strong institutional commitment to the achievement of excellence and diversity among its faculty and staff. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.",
